    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is anchored by **Trevor Story** (75.93) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92), both of whom capitalize on high-upside matchups against favorable arms. **Trevor Story** benefits immensely from a 5.22 xERA opposing starter and a significant wind-out boost, pushing his projection well into the elite tier despite his typical reliance on volume. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** leverages a robust 14% platoon edge against Zac Gallen, combined with strong SP skill metrics that elevate his floor. **Mickey Moniak** (68.75) also commands attention as a high-value play; his 14% platoon advantage against Will Warren effectively masks his base projection, making him an ideal candidate to capitalize on the weak opposing arm.\n\nThe decision to bench **Cole Young** (51.19) was the most difficult in this slate, as he sat just outside the active threshold compared to the primary lineup. While **Cole Young** offers defensive stability, his projected batting order spot of #7 significantly penalized his raw efficiency score compared to the aggressive, top-of-the-order positioning we are targeting with **James Wood** (64.64) and **Brice Turang** (57.55). We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Jose Caballero**, whose score of 60.52 is fragile; if he slips out of the #8 hole or if we see unexpected defensive shifts, his value could plummet due to a stiff 13% dynamic platoon penalty against Tomoyuki Sugano. Additionally, while **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor** are locked in as starters, both face left-handed starters with xERAs that are trending lower than the league average, requiring us to be diligent about late-breaking weather or lineup changes that could necessitate a pivot to the bench depth provided by **Austin Riley** or **Seiya Suzuki**.",
